1
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:02,961
NENAVATH MOHAN: Hi Sathish,

2
00:00:02,961 --> 00:00:04,462
Do you all celebrate Teej?

3
00:00:04,462 --> 00:00:04,921
MEGHAVATH SATHISH: (Yes, we) celebrate.

4
00:00:05,171 --> 00:00:05,797
You celebrate Teej festival?

5
00:00:05,922 --> 00:00:07,966
Oh...that is the highlight (important) festival!

6
00:00:08,007 --> 00:00:09,384
Because our side doesn't celebrate it

7
00:00:09,384 --> 00:00:10,635
since we are in surrounded by the city.

8
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:11,886
So we do not celebrate that festival.

9
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:13,972
So can you explain how you celebrate?

10
00:00:13,972 --> 00:00:16,808
So that I can share about our side also.

11
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:19,811
So can you explain how you celebrate?

12
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:21,521
I think we should try it once on our side.

13
00:00:22,313 --> 00:00:25,024
All the village girls meet in one place.

14
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:26,609
You know, wheat.

15
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:27,736
Hmm...OK...OK...								  

16
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:30,405
It (wheat) is sowed in the soil

17
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:31,197
till it germinates,

18
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:32,323
It falls.

19
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:33,324
Hmm...OK...

20
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,368
Water is brought for them

21
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:37,120
in the morning and in the evening.

22
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,372
By water source and feed them daily.

23
00:00:39,372 --> 00:00:40,165
Okay-Okay.

24
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:42,208
Is that nine day-long festival, right?

25
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:44,627
For nine days, during mornings and evenings,

26
00:00:44,627 --> 00:00:46,463
those girls water the plants,

27
00:00:46,629 --> 00:00:48,548
and performing pooja.

28
00:00:48,965 --> 00:00:49,841
After nine days,

29
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:51,134
wheat seedlings are floated into ponds.

30
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:52,594
Then they sit near the pond,

31
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:54,637
and eat the food they would have brought,

32
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:55,972
and spend a happy time, and return.

33
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:59,100
Right...that's highlight festival for Lambadis.

34
00:00:59,601 --> 00:01:01,728
Teej is a superb festival.

35
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:04,230
For our community, Teej is the best!

36
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:04,981
Best, isn't it?

37
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:08,610
We should proudly say that Teej is ours.

38
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:11,654
But what about people outside of Hyderabad?

39
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:14,324
No one in the surrounding areas celebrate.

40
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,160
But it should be celebrated those surrounding areas.

41
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:19,287
This is my small wish.

42
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:20,914
But let's see if it'll be happen or not...

43
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:25,043
In Nizambad, Adilabad, Warangal—

44
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:26,002
in those areas,

45
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:29,047
In those areas, maximum...

46
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:33,593
This (festival) is only in those areas.

47
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:35,094
In Rangareddy and Mahabubnagar,

48
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:36,179
Teej isn't celebrated.

49
00:01:36,262 --> 00:01:39,265
There are only normal festivals here.

50
00:01:39,265 --> 00:01:40,892
Seethla is celebrated on your side?

51
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:42,352
‘Seethla is celebrated on our side.’

52
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:44,020
But it's not called Seethla.

53
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:45,271
It isn't called Seethla

54
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:46,648
as it's called Gharegharer pooja.

55
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:47,482
Gharegharer pooja...how to celebrate seethla on your side

56
00:01:47,482 --> 00:01:48,691
How do you celebrate Seethla on your side?

57
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:50,944
‘How do we do it on our side?’

58
00:01:51,069 --> 00:01:53,112
Tanda goes to the forest,

59
00:01:53,112 --> 00:01:55,073
sculpts a stone deity idol,...

60
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:55,782
'Hmm...'

61
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:58,743
sacrifice a goat before it.

62
00:01:58,743 --> 00:02:00,286
What do you do?

63
00:02:00,286 --> 00:02:03,122
Cattle and buffaloes belong to Tanda.

64
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:04,249
They revolve around the deity.

65
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:06,876
The way this festival is celebrated on our side—

66
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:07,877
They place a ston

67
00:02:07,877 --> 00:02:08,878
and put neem branches over it—

68
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:09,546
believing that to be the deity.

69
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:11,381
One is Sevalal, and one is Mariamma.

70
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:13,633
Hmm...Bhog is offered to Sevalal.

71
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,635
Usually, a goat is sacrificed in front of Mariamma.

72
00:02:16,052 --> 00:02:17,178
This is our Ghargharer pooja.

73
00:02:17,178 --> 00:02:20,223
But five or six families celebrate together.

74
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:21,266
Sacrifies a goat.

75
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:23,643
Cook overnight, sit, eat happily and enjoy.

76
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:24,686
It's Seethla on your side-

77
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:25,645
Ghargharer pooja on our side.

78
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:27,313
This is the difference between these two.

79
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:28,940
That is the matter.
